llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: a switch's range compare carries the sum of the clusters still to test, as 3.7 (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION in SelectionDAGBuilder's
lowerWorkItem. r246129 (llvm-project 08cb4fc688a9, 2015-08-27) and
r246522 (511298b91951, 2015-09-01), both first released in LLVM 3.8,
make the false edge of a case cluster's compare carry the unhandled
clusters plus the default's share, subtracting a cluster before its
compare is emitted. 3.7 gives the false edge the sum of the clusters
still to be tested without the default's share, a cluster leaves the
sum where its compare is emitted, and an empty sum is left to
BranchProbabilityInfo. This sits on top of switchjt-01 (D66). 0x1af030
and 0x1af3c0 are equal to the base in the prebuilt 3.7.1's module and
22 of 59 under this line without the patch. With the patch both compile
to the base's bytes, thirteen functions of the module change (seven
toward the base, among them 0x12fd240 from 13 to 49 of 58 and 0x13d2490
from 18 to 41 of 52; five level; one draft away, 0xef65f0 from 4 to 2
of 18) and no matched game row changes (round 233B built and swept this
unconditional form alone; held since round 210B for want of an equal
witness).

diff -ru a/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGBuilder.cpp b/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGBuilder.cpp
--- a/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGBuilder.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGBuilder.cpp
@@ -8981,7 +8981,11 @@
 
   // Compute total probability.
   BranchProbability DefaultProb = W.DefaultProb;
-  BranchProbability UnhandledProbs = DefaultProb;
+  // PS4: the false edge of a range compare carries the sum of the clusters
+  // still to be tested, without the default's share, and a cluster leaves
+  // the sum where its compare is emitted, as 3.7 (r246129 and r246522's
+  // share not taken); an empty sum is BranchProbabilityInfo's.
+  BranchProbability UnhandledProbs = BranchProbability::getZero();
   for (CaseClusterIt I = W.FirstCluster; I <= W.LastCluster; ++I)
     UnhandledProbs += I->Prob;
 
@@ -8997,8 +9001,6 @@
       // Put Cond in a virtual register to make it available from the new blocks.
       ExportFromCurrentBlock(Cond);
     }
-    UnhandledProbs -= I->Prob;
-
     switch (I->Kind) {
       case CC_JumpTable: {
         // FIXME: Optimize away range check based on pivot comparisons.
@@ -9073,8 +9075,12 @@
         }
 
         // The false probability is the sum of all unhandled cases.
+        UnhandledProbs -= I->Prob;
+        BranchProbability FalseProb = UnhandledProbs.isZero()
+                                          ? BranchProbability::getUnknown()
+                                          : UnhandledProbs;
         CaseBlock CB(CC, LHS, RHS, MHS, I->MBB, Fallthrough, CurMBB, I->Prob,
-                     UnhandledProbs);
+                     FalseProb);
 
         if (CurMBB == SwitchMBB)
           visitSwitchCase(CB, SwitchMBB);
